<workflow>
  <name>snmp-trap</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description/>
  <extended_description/>
  <created_user>-</created_user>
  <modified_user>-</modified_user>
  <created_date>2026/10/07 10:00:00.000</created_date>
  <modified_date>2026/10/07 10:00:00.000</modified_date>
  <created_hop_version/>
  <modified_hop_version/>
  <workflow_version/>
  <parameters/>
  <actions>
    <action>
      <repeat>N</repeat>
      <schedulerType>0</schedulerType>
      <intervalSeconds>0</intervalSeconds>
      <intervalMinutes>60</intervalMinutes>
      <DayOfMonth>1</DayOfMonth>
      <weekDay>1</weekDay>
      <minutes>0</minutes>
      <hour>12</hour>
      <doNotWaitOnFirstExecution>N</doNotWaitOnFirstExecution>
      <name>Start</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SPECIAL</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>80</xloc>
      <yloc>400</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
    <action>
      <servername>${SNMP_SERVER}</servername>
      <port>162</port>
      <timeout>5000</timeout>
      <nrretry>1</nrretry>
      <comstring>public</comstring>
      <message>Workflow ${Internal.Workflow.Name} needs attention</message>
      <oid>1.3.6.1.4.1.12345.1</oid>
      <targettype>community</targettype>
      <user/>
      <passphrase/>
      <engineid/>
      <name>Send trap</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SNMP_TRAP</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>272</xloc>
      <yloc>400</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
    <action>
      <loglevel>Basic</loglevel>
      <logsubject/>
      <logmessage>SNMP trap sent.</logmessage>
      <name>Done</name>
      <description/>
      <type>WRITE_TO_LOG</type>
      <attributes/>
      <xloc>464</xloc>
      <yloc>400</yloc>
      <parallel>N</parallel>
      <attributes_hac/>
    </action>
  </actions>
  <hops>
    <hop>
      <from>Start</from>
      <to>Send trap</to>
      <evaluation>Y</evaluation>
      <unconditional>Y</unconditional>
      <enabled>Y</enabled>
    </hop>
    <hop>
      <from>Send trap</from>
      <to>Done</to>
      <evaluation>Y</evaluation>
      <unconditional>N</unconditional>
      <enabled>Y</enabled>
    </hop>
  </hops>
  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>The Snmp Trap action sends an SNMP trap to a network management system, for example to raise an alert when a workflow fails.
It supports community based (SNMP v1/v2c) and user based (SNMP v3) targets.

This sample sends a trap with a message to the SNMP manager in the SNMP_SERVER variable.</note>
      <markdown>N</markdown>
      <notetype>GENERAL</notetype>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>11</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>14</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>58</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>90</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>201</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>232</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>251</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>14</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>58</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>90</bordercolorblue>
      <xloc>80</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>640</width>
      <height>120</height>
    </notepad>
    <notepad>
      <note>Requires setup: this sample needs an SNMP manager that receives traps. Set the SNMP_SERVER variable, and the community string and OID your manager expects, before running it.
This sample is excluded from the samples integration tests.</note>
      <markdown>N</markdown>
      <notetype>GENERAL</notetype>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>11</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>110</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>50</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>255</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>220</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>180</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>230</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>126</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>34</bordercolorblue>
      <xloc>80</xloc>
      <yloc>168</yloc>
      <width>640</width>
      <height>70</height>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
  <attributes/>
</workflow>
